Usage:
  nucleus new <project_name> [flags]

Create a new project scaffold: go.mod pinned to this release, a composition-root main.go, nucleus.yml and an empty migrations directory. The mvc and api templates generate no feature code; the suite template carries a worked shop module on the Quark ORM with the Orbit admin panel mounted.

Arguments:
  <project_name>  Directory created under --out; also the default module path suffix (example.com/<project_name>)

Templates (--template):
  mvc    Full-stack: default subsystems, rbac_policy.csv and the driver import for --db (default)
  api    Core-only: WithoutDefaults(), no admin, storage, mail or authz
  suite  Nucleus + Quark + Orbit wired together: a shop module on the Quark ORM, the admin panel under /admin, Data Studio and the live SQL feed (implies --with of all four suite modules)

Suite modules (--with, comma-separated):
  orbit            admin panel (github.com/jcsvwinston/orbit): the admin panel mounted under /admin with its own login gate, Data Studio and the live observability feed
  quark            ORM (github.com/jcsvwinston/quark): the Quark ORM (Active Record models, migrations from the model registry) for the application's domain
  quarkbridge      observability bridge (github.com/jcsvwinston/orbit/quarkbridge): a Quark middleware that publishes every statement on the observability bus, so orbit's live feed shows the SQL correlated to the request
  quarkdatasource  Data Studio adapter (github.com/jcsvwinston/orbit/quarkdatasource): the adapter that backs orbit's Data Studio with Quark models, so /admin browses and edits them

Databases (--db):
  sqlite     sqlite://app.db and drivers/sqlite (default)
  postgres   drivers/postgres (also: postgresql, pg)
  mysql      drivers/mysql
  sqlserver  drivers/mssql (also: mssql)
  oracle     drivers/oracle

Flags:
  -db string
    	Database engine the project starts on (sqlite, postgres, mysql, sqlserver, oracle): its driver module is required and imported (default "sqlite")
  -force
    	Overwrite scaffold files if the project directory exists
  -module string
    	Go module path (default: example.com/<project_name>)
  -offline
    	Do not touch the network: skip the go get of the driver and suite modules and the go mod tidy (run them yourself before go run .)
  -out string
    	Parent directory where the project folder will be created (default ".")
  -port int
    	HTTP port in nucleus.yml (default 8080)
  -template string
    	Starter template (mvc: full-stack, api: lightweight core-only, suite: Nucleus + Quark + Orbit wired together) (default "mvc")
  -with string
    	Suite modules to fetch and wire, comma-separated (orbit, quark, quarkbridge, quarkdatasource); --template suite implies all four

Examples:
  nucleus new blog --module github.com/acme/blog
  nucleus new svc --template api --port 9090
  nucleus new shop --db postgres
  nucleus new blog --with orbit   # the admin panel mounted under /admin
  nucleus new store --template suite --db sqlite
  nucleus new lab --offline   # no go get / go mod tidy; run them yourself

The driver module for --db and every suite module --with names are imported by the generated code and resolved on the spot (go get from the module proxy at their published tags, then go mod tidy), so the project builds as written; --offline skips all of it and hands the commands back as the next step.

The suite tags Nucleus before Orbit: right after a Nucleus release the orbit tag may still pin the previous Nucleus minor; go keeps the higher of the two and the next Orbit tag closes the gap.
